Lab 9: Create Users and Assign Them to Groups
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Create multiple users in Ansible Automation Platform • Assign users to different groups based on their organizational roles • Configure appropriate permissions for user groups • Test user access to resources and validate security controls • Understand the relationship between users, groups, and role-based access control (RBAC) • Implement best practices for user management in automation environments

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of Linux user management concepts • Familiarity with Ansible Automation Platform components (Controller and Hub) • Knowledge of role-based access control (RBAC) principles • Understanding of organizational roles and responsibilities • Basic web browser navigation skills • Completed previous labs covering Ansible Automation Platform installation and basic configuration

Lab Environment
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with Ansible Automation Platform already installed. Simply click Start Lab to access your environment - no need to build your own VM or install software.

Your lab environment includes: • Ansible Automation Controller (AWX) accessible via web interface • Ansible Automation Hub for content management • Pre-configured network connectivity • Administrative access to create and manage users

